====================================================================================================
G1. shear: the background has none, a well has plenty (symbolic strain tensors)
====================================================================================================
  homologous u = lambda r : volume strain = 3*lambda, shear^2 = 0
  well infall u ~ -u0 r^-n : volume strain = 6.1714e+19*3.0857e+19**n*u_0*(1.0/r)**n*(0.5*n - 1.0)/r, shear^2 = 1.26953926533333e+39*9.52154449e+38**n*r**(-2*n - 2)*u_0**2*(0.5*n**2 + 1.0*n + 0.5)
  [PASS] G1 isotropic (Hubble) deformation has exactly zero shear at every density; non-homologous infall has shear^2 > 0 -- so a shear-rigid, bulk-soft solid is NOT a function of the local state and the matching theorem does not apply to it
  a solid resists what the background never does; that is the whole escape.

====================================================================================================
G2. linear regime: soft, and colder into the past (c_L^2 = 4 mu_0 / 3 rho ~ a^3)
====================================================================================================
  plane-wave delta = uniaxial strain: shear = (2/3)|delta| -> for delta << s_0 the medium is in its soft branch.  Choose mu_0 by today's longitudinal speed c_L(0).
  c_L(0) =     5 km/s: c_L^2(rec) = 2.1e-19, c_L(z=3) =   0.6 km/s, lambda_J today =   0.7 Mpc
  c_L(0) =    20 km/s: c_L^2(rec) = 3.4e-18, c_L(z=3) =   2.5 km/s, lambda_J today =   3.0 Mpc
  c_L(0) =    40 km/s: c_L^2(rec) = 1.4e-17, c_L(z=3) =   5.0 km/s, lambda_J today =   5.9 Mpc
  c_L(0) =   100 km/s: c_L^2(rec) = 8.6e-17, c_L(z=3) =  12.5 km/s, lambda_J today =  14.8 Mpc
  [PASS] G2 for c_L(0) <= 40 km/s the solid is CMB-cold by > 1e-8 margin (c_L^2(rec) < 1e-13) and forest-cold at z = 3 (c_L < 5 km/s): the (1+z)^3 heating that killed the condensates runs the other way for a constant modulus
  (the constant-c_s^2 control of the pincer, 4 km/s, lost only 7% at k = 10 h/Mpc; this history is colder than that at every z > 0.)

====================================================================================================
G3. the shield without pressure: radial infall of a hardening solid into a fixed L* MOND well
====================================================================================================
  model: Lagrangian shell at initial radius R0 (mean density) falls to r; compression ratio rho/rho_bar = (R0/r)^2 / (dr/dR0).
  Equilibrium: the elastic shear stress gradient balances gravity, mu(s) s / r ~ rho g.  With mu = mu_0 [1 + (s/s_0)^n] and s = the deviatoric strain
  of the shell (|eps_rr - eps_thth| ~ ln(rho/rho_bar) for large compressions), the stall compression solves mu(s) s = rho_bar (rho/rho_bar) g r.
  hardening law: mu = mu_0 delta^p (p > 1): dust-soft at delta < 1 (linear cosmology untouched), stiffening under compression;
  equilibrium delta^(p-1) ln delta = g r / (mu_0/rho_bar).  A deeper well compresses it further: the cap is ordered by g r, i.e. by well depth.
